Subject: [PATCH 0011] machine: stop at a virtual time; input while so paused

# melco-nav-emu core patch.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# Copyright (c) 2026 melco-nav-emu contributors
# Modifies GPL-licensed QEMU sources; applied by scripts/qemu.sh.

Harness hooks for deterministic headless runs (bootcheck).  Every machine
gets two QOM properties, used with qom-get/qom-set on /machine:

  x-vclock-ns   QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL now (read-only)
  x-stop-at-ns  pause the VM (RUN_STATE_PAUSED, QMP STOP event) when the
                virtual clock reaches this time; negative disarms

Under -icount with sleep=off the pause lands on the same guest instruction
every run.  The timer callback stops every vCPU itself (in the vCPU thread
current_cpu is NULL between TBs, so vm_stop() alone leaves it running until
the main loop pauses it) and inhibits icount's idle clock warp until the VM
runs again (otherwise, before the main loop sets the run state, the stopped
vCPU counts as idle, the clock jumps to the next device deadline and device
timers may run: a host-time race).  Once x-stop-at-ns has been used, a VM paused that way accepts
input events (send-key, input-send-event) instead of dropping them, so a key
reaches the board's input handler at an exact virtual time; the key-up of
send-key's hold-time follows on QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL as upstream.  Nothing
here is visible to the guest.

